      "hints": [
        "Combine fractions over $\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)$.",
        "Expand numerator to $(1 + \\cos\\theta)^2 + \\sin^2\\theta = 2 + 2\\cos\\theta = 2(1 + \\cos\\theta)$.",
        "Cancel $(1 + \\cos\\theta)$ to get $\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Combine the two fractions on the left-hand side over a common denominator:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{(1 + \\cos\\theta)^2 + \\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)}$$",
        "Expand the squared binomial and apply $\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = 1$ in the numerator:\n$$\\text{Numerator} = 1 + 2\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = 1 + 2\\cos\\theta + 1 = 2 + 2\\cos\\theta = 2(1 + \\cos\\theta)$$",
        "Cancel the common factor $(1 + \\cos\\theta)$ with the denominator:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{2(1 + \\cos\\theta)}{\\sin\\theta(1 + \\cos\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta} = \\text{RHS}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Identity Proof": "Forms common denominator (M1). Expands and uses Pythagorean identity (M1). Cancels factor to obtain $\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta}$ (A1)."
        },
