      "hints": [
        "Use identity: $\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta} = \\frac{3}{\\cos\\theta} \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\frac{2}{3}$.",
        "Solve in $[0^\\circ, 360^\\circ]$ to find $\\theta = 33.7^\\circ, 213.7^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the proven identity into the equation:\n$$\\frac{2}{\\sin\\theta} = \\frac{3}{\\cos\\theta} \\implies 2\\cos\\theta = 3\\sin\\theta \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\frac{2}{3}$$",
        "Find all solutions for $\\theta$ in the range $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 360^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta_1 = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\approx 33.69^\\circ \\approx 33.7^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta_2 = 180^\\circ + 33.69^\\circ \\approx 213.7^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 33.7^\\circ, \\quad 213.7^\\circ)$$"
      ],
